<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Datasets</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our models are trained using the GSM8k-Aug and GSM8k-Aug-NL datasets introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. (2023)</a></cite>, which augment the training set of the GSM8k <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite> using GPT4 and provide a separate validation split.
The golden traces in the datasets are split into discrete steps. GSM8k-Aug traces consist only of succinct statements such as <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;&lt;600*30/100=180&gt;&gt;; &lt;&lt;600*10/100=60&gt;&gt;</span>. The questions and answers in the NL (Natural Language) subset are identical, however the steps are formulated in natural language: <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">600 x 30/100 = 180 employees were promoted.; 600 x 10/100 = 60 employees received a bonus.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.tab1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
